hub.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108954#issuecomment-3119813988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108954","id":3119813988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc659JVk","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T17:58:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T21:04:05Z","body":"> This would only work for stretch mode Viewport, wouldn't it? It also ignores the size override settings, is that alright?\r\n\r\nI've tested the commit with the `disabled` stretch mode and it still works. However, this means the size override does not affect the recording resolution anymore, but this was existing behavior when using the `viewport` stretch mode already.\r\n\r\nI guess we should use the `size_override` project setting when the stretch mode is `disabled` or `canvas_items`, and `size` when the stretch mode is `viewport` to fully preserve existing behavior.\r\n\r\n**Edit:** I've pushed a third commit that does the above. The output video size is also now printed on startup as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues